# Required environment variables for verdant-command-center-preview
# All variables are VITE_-prefixed and safe for client-side exposure.
#
# ⚠️  NEVER add SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY or any secret key here.
#     Only anon/publishable keys are permitted in client builds.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://<project-ref>.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="<supabase-anon-key>"
VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="<supabase-project-ref>"

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Paddle
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Live charges are possible only with a `live_` token on the production
# hostnames (see below). Local development cannot complete a checkout: the
# local frontend talks to the production backend, whose price lookup uses the
# live catalog once PAYMENTS_ENVIRONMENT is live, so a local `test_` client would
# be a sandbox/live hybrid. Treat local checkout as unavailable. Verdant has no
# preview or staging environment.
#
# VITE_PAYMENTS_CLIENT_TOKEN is the CANONICAL publishable client-side token
# for the Lovable-managed Paddle lane (see docs/billing.md). It is safe for
# client builds. A `test_` token (`test_` + exactly 27 letters/digits) opens
# Paddle sandbox checkout on any host; a malformed one fails closed. A
# `live_` token (Paddle's shape: `live_` + exactly 27 letters/digits; any other
# `live_` value is malformed and fails closed) opens live checkout ONLY on
# verdantgrowdiary.com and www.verdantgrowdiary.com; on any other hostname (for
# example localhost) it fails closed and checkout stays unavailable. Production
# builds use the token committed in .env.production, which must be a well-formed
# live_ token: the prebuild gate rejects a sandbox or malformed token, and a
# build where the bundled token differs from that file. The VITE_PADDLE_* set
# below is the deprecated BYO-era naming, retained only for older local setups.
#
# Never put server-only secrets (API keys, webhook signing secrets) in this
# file — they are configured via the Lovable Cloud secrets store, not .env.

VITE_PAYMENTS_CLIENT_TOKEN=""

# Deprecated BYO-era client vars (superseded by VITE_PAYMENTS_CLIENT_TOKEN).
# That legacy path stays sandbox-only and refuses "live" or "production":
VITE_PADDLE_ENVIRONMENT="sandbox"
VITE_PADDLE_CLIENT_TOKEN=""
VITE_PADDLE_PRICE_PRO_MONTHLY=""
VITE_PADDLE_PRICE_PRO_ANNUAL=""
VITE_PADDLE_PRICE_FOUNDER_LIFETIME=""

# Server-only Paddle secrets (configured via Lovable Cloud → Secrets, NOT here).
# Canonical Lovable lane (payments-webhook / paddle-portal-session /
# get-paddle-price — see docs/billing.md and docs/paddle-paid-launch-runbook.md):
#   PADDLE_SANDBOX_API_KEY            # gateway connection key (sandbox)
#   PADDLE_LIVE_API_KEY               # gateway connection key (live)
#   PAYMENTS_SANDBOX_WEBHOOK_SECRET   # webhook SIGNING secret (NOT the API key);
#   PAYMENTS_LIVE_WEBHOOK_SECRET      #   verifies Paddle-Signature on the RAW body
#   PAYMENTS_ENVIRONMENT              # exactly "live" for the production live
#                                     #   release: read and confirmed in the
#                                     #   production backend before get-paddle-price
#                                     #   is deployed and before checkout is exposed.
#                                     #   Never infer it from the client token. A
#                                     #   live client with a sandbox selector is a
#                                     #   forbidden hybrid.
#   LOVABLE_API_KEY                   # Lovable gateway auth
# Legacy BYO audit sink (paddle-webhook only):
#   PADDLE_ENVIRONMENT          # permanently "sandbox" (audit lane only; it
#                               #   never handles live events)
#   PADDLE_WEBHOOK_SECRET       # used by the paddle-webhook edge function
#                               # to verify signatures against the raw body

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Production error reporting (Sentry browser SDK, client only)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave EMPTY. With no DSN the reporter never loads the SDK. To turn reporting
# on, create the DSN in Sentry and set VITE_SENTRY_DSN in the Cloudflare
# Workers Builds environment. Do not commit a DSN. The reporter stays off
# unless the build mode is exactly production (a missing or unknown mode stays
# off) and the hostname is verdantgrowdiary.com or www.verdantgrowdiary.com.
# The DSN host must be one of the Sentry ingest origins in the report-only
# CSP connect-src list. Any other host is refused.
# Outgoing events drop user fields, IP, request bodies, cookies, headers and
# query strings; redact exception text; and drop breadcrumbs that carry
# content. Non-http schemes, including vbscript:, are rejected.
# Direct browser requests still expose the source IP at the transport layer.
# Sentry-side IP retention is NOT_MEASURED.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=""
